    {
      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "Start with the single idea the whole topic rests on. In most US states, a landlord can only take deductions for actual damage, not for normal wear and tear. Normal wear and tear is the ordinary aging you would expect from simply living in a place. Faded paint, a few small nail holes, lightly worn carpet in the walkways. That is the landlord's cost of doing business, not yours.",
